@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide methods
left to right direction

package "Geographic Query Engine" {

    class Station {
        +stationId
        +name
        +country
        +latitude
        +longitude
        +timeZoneGroup
    }

    class StationIndex {
        +byLatitude
        +byLongitude
        +byTimeZoneGroup
        +searchByWindow()
        +searchByRadius()
    }

    class GeoQuery {
        +queryId
        +queryType  ' radius | window | nearest
        +parameters
        +resultSet
    }

    class GeoQueryEngine {
        +executeQuery()
        +applyFilters()
        +computeDistance()
        +formatResults()
    }

    class Planner {
        +submitQuery()
        +viewResults()
    }

}

Planner "1" --> "1" GeoQueryEngine : uses >
GeoQueryEngine "1" --> "1" GeoQuery : executes >
GeoQueryEngine "1" --> "1" StationIndex : accesses >
StationIndex "1" --> "0..*" Station : references >

note bottom of GeoQuery
A GeoQuery defines the type "of" spatial search:
- radius (stations within X km)
- window (stations between lat/lon bounds)
- nearest (closest N stations)
Results are sorted deterministically.
end note

note right of StationIndex
StationIndex wraps multiple AVL/BST trees:
- byLatitude
- byLongitude
- byTimeZoneGroup
Used for efficient spatial lookups.
end note

note right of GeoQueryEngine
Combines results from multiple indexes,
applies geographic filters and distance
computations (e.g., Haversine).
end note

@enduml
